```mdl
decision D-49: Before the client is up, the app draws the pill from the names the last visit cached, and the live pill replaces it in the same frame once it knows its diagram. Fills in [D-48].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-1.5, BootShell]
  why: The framework renders nothing until the client worker connects, about 550 ms into a warm load; the shell paints at about 100 ms, and the shell and live pill share one set of parts, so the swap does not move a pixel.
  rejected:
    - A static HTML pill in index.html: paints earlier, but it is a second copy of the pill's styling that drifts.
```

```mdl
decision D-50: Plugins, identity and space open start together, and the app mounts without suspending; each diagram remembers the objects it reached, and its next open loads them in one batch. Fills in [D-48].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-1.6, DiagramRoot]
  why: A suspension during boot costs React's reveal throttle (about 300 ms), and the diagram's objects form a chain (drawing, canvas, scene, layout, model) in which each reference cost a round trip to the worker.
```

```mdl
decision D-51: The diagram's frame (its toolbars and panels) draws at once and its content loads a moment later, both in the boot shell and in the live diagram.
  date: 2026-11-15
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-1.5, BootShell]
```

```mdl
decision D-52: The boot shell draws a copy of the frame the live diagram drew as it last opened, with the scene's layers removed, and only with the stylesheet it was drawn with. Fills in [D-51].
  date: 2026-11-15
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-1.5, BootShell, DrawingView]
  why: The copy matches the live frame exactly, whatever tools, panels and theme the diagram has, and it adds nothing to the code that loads before first paint.
  rejected:
    - Placeholder toolbars drawn by hand: a second copy of the canvas editor's frame that drifts, and the tools differ per diagram.
    - The canvas editor's own toolbars in the boot shell: they need its whole editor and its scene, and they grow the code that loads before first paint.
```

```mdl
decision D-53: The live diagram's article stays as it is: it finds its canvas, scene and document loaded on its first render, so it has nothing to draw ahead of. Fills in [D-51].
  date: 2026-11-15
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-1.5]
  why: Measured on warm loads, the article first renders within 2 ms of the drawing reaching the space's query, with every object it reads already loaded; the time before that is the drawing reaching the query.
```

```mdl
decision D-54: The drawing list stays pending until the diagram the URL or the last visit names loads or fails to. Fills in [D-48].
