  supersedes: D-64
  affects: [F-6.1, F-6.2, F-6.3]
  why: The panel already reports a failure and offers to start over, so the toast and the app's own failure rules, and the card of [D-65], have nothing left to do.
```

```mdl
decision D-75: While the app joins a space it shows the join dialog where it would show its "Opening…" loading text. Only joins are covered.
  date: 2026-11-15
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-1.5, F-6.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-76: An invitation link's boot shell draws a still copy of the join dialog as it connects, and the live dialog replaces it once on screen. After a join succeeds the app shows the copy again until the joined space shows; behind the live dialog it shows only the surface. A join started from the space menu does the same. Fills in [D-75].
  date: 2026-11-15
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-1.5, F-6.2, BootShell, JoinShell]
  why: The copy is drawn with react-ui's `Dialog` parts as Composer's panel draws its first step, so the swaps do not show. The join dialog closes before the joined space is ready, so the gap after it is the app's to cover.
  rejected:
    - Keeping plugin-space's join dialog open until it opens the space: `Open` returns before the space is ready, and the panel has no view for a finished join, so it shows a title over an empty body.
```

```mdl
decision D-77: Closing the join panel before its join finishes cancels the invitation. Fills in [D-70].
  date: 2026-11-15
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-6.3, QA-3]
  why: Closing the dialog while it was connecting left the join running, and the space was joined about 20 s later while the user was in another one. The panel is Composer's too, so Composer gains the same fix.
```

```mdl
decision D-78: Started without an invitation, the app boots straight to its shell; started with one, it boots straight to the join dialog. The shell is always behind the dialog, so closing the dialog shows the shell at once.
  date: 2026-11-15
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-1.5, F-6.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-79: The boot shell is always drawn, without names for a space the last visit did not show, and sits under dialogs and toasts. The still join dialog is a separate overlay above it, drawn in the same paint on a link, removed once a live dialog is on screen, and drawn again after a join succeeds until the joined diagram replaces the shell. Where nothing covers the app before a space shows, it draws only its surface. Fills in [D-78].
  date: 2026-11-15
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-76
  affects: [F-1.5, F-6.2, BootShell, JoinShell]
  why: Keeping the shell under the dialog is what makes closing it immediate, and the separate overlay lets the live dialog replace only the copy. Drawing both in one paint avoids a frame of shell without the dialog.
  rejected:
    - Moving the shell above the live dialog and hiding it there: the live dialog's scrim and toasts would sit under it.
```
